{"name":"Cheater","hex":"#eeb15d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who cheats; something that cheats.","Synonym of adulterer."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An escheater."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheater (Pom Poko album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cheater is the second studio album by Norwegian post-punk band Pom Poko. The album was originally scheduled for release on 6 November 2020, but was moved to 15 January 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/47/Pom_Poko_-_Cheater.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheater_(Pom_Poko_album)","wikidata":"Q106011641"},{"title":"Cheater (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cheater\" is a song written by Michael Jackson and Greg Phillinganes and was originally slated to appear on Jackson's seventh studio album, Bad (1987), but it was removed from the track listing for unknown reasons. The song was officially released on November 16, 2004, as part of The Ultimate Collection album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/MJ_Cheater_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheater_(song)","wikidata":"Q1095079"},{"title":"Cheating","blocks":[{"text":"Cheating generally describes various actions designed to subvert or disobey rules in order to obtain unfair advantages without being noticed. This includes acts of bribery, cronyism and nepotism in any situation where individuals are given preference using inappropriate criteria. The rules infringed may be explicit, or they may be from an unwritten code of conduct based on morality, ethics or custom, making the identification of cheating conduct a potentially subjective process. Cheating can refer specifically to infidelity, where arranged or consensual relationships, that often come with a social contract, are violated. Someone who is known for cheating is referred to as a cheat in British English, and a cheater in American English."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheating","wikidata":"Q19"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cheating.JPG/500px-Cheating.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cheating.JPG/1280px-Cheating.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cheating.JPG/500px-Cheating.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" A small cheat sheet can be used to cheat during an academic examination.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheating.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg/500px-Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg/1280px-Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg/500px-Lance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 2012 investigation by the United States Anti-Doping Agency (USADA) found that Lance Armstrong had used banned performance-enhancing drugs over the course of his cycling career.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALance_Armstrong--2002--w.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/18220829_An_ingenious_cheat_-_bowling_-_The_Georgian_For_the_Country_%28Savannah%29.jpg/500px-18220829_An_ingenious_cheat_-_bowling_-_The_Georgian_For_the_